---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Tile" description="Visual pattern for a single interaction; Box for static surfaces or various controls.">
  <h1>Tile</h1>
  <p class="lede"><strong>Strict invariant:</strong> each Tile has exactly one interactive intent. A Tile is never a static surface. For static content or multiple independent controls, use <a href="/en/components/box">Box</a>.</p>
  <p>Tile is a visual recipe that semantic components apply to the correct native element. The TileLink, TileButton, TileCheckbox, and TileRadioGroup demos and contracts live alongside Link, Button, Checkbox, and RadioGroup.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/en/components/card">Card</a> guide compares these roots with Box on real content, news, product, link, action, selection and metrics cards.</p>

  <h2>Choose by behavior</h2>
  <div class="sk-table-scroll">
  <table class="sk-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Necesidad</th><th>Component</th><th>Contrato nativo</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Static content or multiple controls</td><td><a href="/en/components/box">Box</a></td><td>The element chosen by the user.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Navigate to a destination</td><td><a href="/en/components/link">Link</a></td><td><code>TileLink</code> uses <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Execute an action</td><td><a href="/en/components/button">Button</a></td><td><code>TileButton</code> uses <code>&lt;button type="button"&gt;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Seleccionar independientemente</td><td><a href="/en/components/checkbox">Checkbox</a></td><td><code>TileCheckbox</code> uses <code>&lt;input type="checkbox"&gt;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Choose an exclusive option</td><td><a href="/en/components/radio-group">RadioGroup</a></td><td><code>TileRadioGroup</code> uses <code>&lt;input type="radio"&gt;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Show or hide details (one or more)</td><td><a href="/en/components/accordion">Accordion</a></td><td><code>&lt;button&gt;</code> trigger; one or more Tile disclosures</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>



  <h2>Contratos</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Link and button do not require enhancer: the browser already provides their behavior.</li>
    <li>Checkbox, radio group and Accordion retain real inputs or buttons. Its vanilla enhancers read the <code>data-part</code> hooks documented in the semantic components. A single disclosure is Accordion with one item.</li>
    <li>Do not nest interactive controls inside a Tile. If independent actions are needed, use <a href="/en/components/box">Box</a> and leave the controls as siblings.</li>
    <li>React bindings render the same semantic contract; They do not use the Vanilla enhancer.</li>
    <li>All Tiles accept <code>data-padding</code> with <code>none</code>, <code>xs</code>, <code>sm</code>, <code>md</code>, <code>lg</code> or <code>xl</code>; React exposes the same value as <code>padding</code>. The default is <code>md</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
